      "source": "Simon Willison",
      "media": "text",
      "title": "ttok 1.0",
      "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/9/ttok/",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-09T00:34:43.000Z",
      "snippet": " <p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/ttok/releases/tag/1.0\">ttok 1.0</a></p> <p>I released <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/8/ttok/\">ttok 0.4</a>, ran <code>uv tool upgrade ttok</code>, piped a file into the new version... and realized that it was defaulting to the GPT-4 tokenizer when it should very clearly default to GPT-5/GPT-6 instead!</p> <p>I figured switching the default was a reasonable excuse to finally ship a 1.0.</p> <p>OpenAI haven't actually co",
      "enclosure": null
